<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A0.F11.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 11</span>: </span><span id="A0.F11.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Additional selected samples from our 512<math id="A0.F11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math>512 and 256<math id="A0.F11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math>256 resolution DiT-XL/2 models.<span id="A0.F11.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> We use a classifier-free guidance scale of 6.0 for the <math id="A0.F11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="512\times 512" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>512</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>512</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">512\times 512</annotation></semantics></math> model and 4.0 for the <math id="A0.F11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="256\times 256" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>256</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>256</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">256\times 256</annotation></semantics></math> model. Both models use the ft-EMA VAE decoder.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
  
